                              "text":  "Amendment 2026-08-28c - 28b reversed, formula evaluated. PRE-RUN.\r\n\r\nAmendment 2026-08-28b withdrew predictions P1/P2 citing an on-disk int8\r\nsize of ~3.16 GB. The authoritative pin value contradicts that:\r\n\r\n  W4 = ir_bytes(Qwen3-4B-int4-ov) = 2,290,768,181\r\n  W8 = ir_bytes(Qwen3-4B-int8-ov) = 4,054,072,455\r\n  W8/W4 = 1.770\r\n\r\nThe original bits-per-param derivation was correct; the disk delta was\r\nthe error. Amendment 28b is REVERSED. Both moves remain in the record:\r\na prediction withdrawn on bad evidence and restored on good evidence is\r\na different object from one never questioned, and the difference is\r\nauditable.\r\n\r\n  KV_nominal  = 73,728 B/token    (u8, run 41e419bd)\r\n  KV_resident = 171,532 B/token   (u8 total, run 41e419bd)\r\n\r\n  ratio_lo(n) = (W8 + 171532n) / (W4 + 171532n)\r\n  ratio_hi(n) = (W8 +  73728n) / (W4 +  73728n)\r\n\r\nP2\u0027. Observed int8:int4 decode ratio falls inside [ratio_lo, ratio_hi]:\r\n\r\n       n =  2,000    1.670 - 1.723\r\n       n =  5,000    1.560 - 1.663\r\n       n = 12,000    1.405 - 1.555\r\n\r\n     The bounds bracket whether the fixed ~95 KB/token workspace\r\n     participates in per-step bandwidth. Observations at the hi bound\r\n     mean it does not move per token; at the lo bound, it does. Either\r\n     answer is a finding about the memory system.\r\n\r\nP2\u0027\u0027. THE TREND, load-bearing: the ratio DECLINES MONOTONICALLY with\r\n     n_cached, because shared KV bytes dilute the weight difference.\r\n     Flat or rising falsifies the additive weights+KV bandwidth model\r\n     regardless of where the point estimates land. Cannot be fitted\r\n     post hoc.\r\n\r\nP1\u0027. int8 resident base exceeds int4\u0027s measured 2.3 GB by\r\n     (W8 - W4) = 1.763 GB, +/- 15%. Predicted int8 base 3.8 - 4.4 GB.\r\n\r\nFALSIFIED IF: any depth falls outside its band by more than 0.15, or\r\nthe trend is non-monotone.\r\n",
